<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diriyah</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dir'iyah, Ad-Dir'iyah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diriyah is a town in Wadi Hanifa on the north-western edge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a>, Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. It was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-saud">Al Saud</a> and capital of the first Saudi state from the 18th century, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-saud">Muhammad ibn Saud</a> allied with the preacher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-abd-al-wahhab">Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab</a> in 1744. Ottoman-Egyptian forces under Ibrahim Pasha destroyed it in 1818. Its mud-brick district of at-Turaif is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diriyah.jpg" alt="Diriyah" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FShbib · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Riyadh_Region_-_Ad_Diriyah.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
